// adversarial-target: false-no-alias-hoist
//
// D-05-05's engineered false-alias control target. `value`'s SHARED (never
// exclusive) borrow chain covers the whole call: deriveAliasFacts (check.go)
// requires an EXCLUSIVE first borrow, so this fixture yields ZERO alias
// facts, and cgen's selectsByPointerLowering (also exclusive-first-gated)
// never selects it either -- production cgen instead selects the sibling
// selectsByPointerLoweringSharedOnly path (emitLinearBorrowedByPointerPlain),
// which lowers this parameter by pointer WITHOUT restrict (a shared loan
// alone never justifies it) and exposes a second, purely-adversarial raw
// pointer parameter (lang_alias_probe) that the unmutated body never reads
// or writes. session.AliasFactMutationRunner is the only thing that ever
// touches that dormant parameter: it injects a FALSE restrict onto the
// primary parameter and rewrites the body to demonstrate the resulting
// observable -O3 hoist, proving control:alias.false_no_alias has a real,
// engineered subject rather than an unexercised name (D-05-38).
module phase5.false_restrict_hoist

export {
  fn touch
}

fn touch(value: Byte) -> Byte {
  let first = borrow value
  first
}
